[[0,1347288,0,32,2,30,"2016-10-15T01:07:56","juggornot","",[],"<p>I went to Subway for lunch because I didn't have time to pack a salad (I'm bad at mornings). Whilst there I witnessed this thing:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://i.sli.mg/NO7u7M.jpg\">https://i.sli.mg/NO7u7M.jpg</a></p>\n<p>So she gave me that pandering &quot;ohaidar xd&quot; smile fats do. This irritated me. I stared unflinchingly forward. She was getting her sandwich finished and ALL I COULD SEE was cheese. Melted cheddar cheese. And mayo. As she was checking out, I began my order. Keep that time in mind, because when the employee was DONE making my sandwich she was still at checkout. The employee just kind of awkwardly put my sandwich on top of the glass case thing and went to the back (they were restocking their trays, maybe hammy ate everything?). She got chips, a 12&quot; sub, and a chocolate chip cookie. But no, wait, they &quot;have PUMPKIN COOKIES now?!?!1 I have to try them!&quot; So she didn't just change from a chocolate chip cookie to a pumpkin cookie she got BOTH (&quot;Try them both, teehee!&quot;). Then she couldn't get her card to read, she reeee'd that she didn't have a chip (I dislike the chip technology myself but virtually every card issuer including my godawful insecure bank has issued chipped cards now ffs) and couldn't get her card to work. By this point I'm just standing there, sandwich in hand, fuming. So she takes out her wallet and hands the cashier some cash from her grubby fat hands (poor guy). Then I FINALLY check out myself, in about 30 seconds, and am on my way.</p>","Ham eats \"\"\"fresh\"\"\" [pic incl]","","fatpeoplehate"],[1,6567952,0,3,0,3,"2016-10-15T03:34:25","Leelem0n","",[],"<p>That sounds absolutely disgusting, though I'm surprised something that big didn't order more.</p>"],[2,6571532,6567952,1,0,1,"2016-10-15T18:14:10","lifting_cat","[e]",[],"<p>Don't worry, that was just its in-between-snacks snack. It'll be back for more.</p>"],[1,6568481,0,6,0,6,"2016-10-15T05:21:40","theepilepticferret","",[],"<p>That must be bordering on a shitlady's calories for the entire day.</p>\n<p>Are you in the US? Canada has had chip technology for several years now and I prefer it to the old swipe cards, especially when it comes to credit cards.</p>"],[1,6569564,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-15T12:04:50","MrSaxoBeetus","",[],"<p>I call bullshit. Where's the Diet Coke? </p>"],[1,6569744,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-15T12:57:47","miss_ann_thrope","",[],"<p>I didn't know they made belts large enough to fit around an obeast's hips.</p>"],[2,6571154,6569744,0,0,0,"2016-10-15T17:14:57","KCshitlady","",[],"<p>Huge belts are all I see in stores! I get mine on Amazon. They're cheaper and cuter anyway.</p>"],[1,6570444,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-15T15:15:28","notafatty2","",[],"<p>I see this all the time, I also see potentially healthy meals being slathered with mayo/ranch. you were so close! but no, a pound of mayo please.</p>"]]
